{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs36 Trace Data Plot\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Automatic plotting of the most recent trace data.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The plot can be generated by either:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Start the trace on next move. A plot is generated once the move is complete.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Start an immediate trace. A plot is generated once the trace is stopped.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The plot can be controlled using a mouse and a keyboard:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Left mouse} \u8211- View the value of a data point. {\pict\pngblip\picw335\pich146\picwgoal5077\pichgoal2213\bin }\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Right mouse} \u8211- Pan the plot.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Scroll at Axis label} \u8211- Zoom in or out of that axis.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Hold Ctrl, then drag Right mouse} \u8211- Boxed zoom.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Double-click Middle mouse} \u8211- Reset zoom.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The units of time and distance data can also be changed.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Time unit can be changed to {\b s} (second) or {\b ms} (milliseconds).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab The unit of distance related variables can be changed to {\b mm} (millimeters), {\b um} (micrometers), or {\b nm} (nanometers). The default unit for distance is {\b any}, which displays the units of the original data.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A new plot is generated every time a trace is done.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 To keep a plot, press \u8216'{\b Open in new window}\u8217' button. This generates the same plot in another window. To reset the zoom amount of a plot, press \u8216'{\b Reset Zoom}\u8217' button. A plot generated in a new window has its own \u8216'Reset Zoom\u8217' button.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 These options can be selected in the controls as below: {\pict\pngblip\picw357\pich104\picwgoal5411\pichgoal1576\bin }\par}
